# Agentic attack detections by ThreatDefence: Cochise
# https://github.com/ThreatDefence/agentic-attack-detections
# Suricata 7 and 8. SID range 3813401-3813415, unused: see below.
# Cochise has no web console and sends no fixed marker to a target. The one network rule is for its SSH client: it
# drives a Kali VM over asyncssh and does not set client_version, so the VM sees the asyncssh default banner
# (andreashappe/cochise at 4db4fded, src/cochise/ssh_connection.py:19; asyncssh 2.24.0 in uv.lock). Any asyncssh
# client sends the same banner: treat a hit as context, and look at what the session runs.

# --- SSH client banner SSH-2.0-AsyncSSH_<version> to an internal SSH server ---
# Covered by the shared asyncssh rule 3813107 in frameworks/hackingbuddygpt/suricata/hackingbuddygpt.rules (port 22),
# which names both tools; Cochise has no rule of its own.
